{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 90,
    "dDurationMs": 4327,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a video about the most important\nalgorithm of all time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4417,
    "dDurationMs": 2933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Fast Fourier Transform or FFT."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7350,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, you use it all the time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9270,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including right now to watch this video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11310,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's used in radar\nand sonar, 5G and WiFi."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15390,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Basically, anytime a signal is processed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17910,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's a good chance that\na Fast Fourier Transform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20100,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is involved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21210,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But on top of all this, the FFT\nwas discovered by scientists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25260,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trying to detect covert\nnuclear weapons tests."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28470,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if they had discovered it sooner,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30540,
    "dDurationMs": 2883,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it may have put a stop\nto the nuclear arms race."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36750,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know I always assumed\nthat the nuclear arms race"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39090,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was inevitable, that once\nthe U.S. dropped atomic bombs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41850,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on Hiroshima and Nagasaki,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43440,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was just unavoidable that\nall the other major powers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45960,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would develop nukes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47370,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But maybe it wasn't because\nit was clear to everyone"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51090,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that nuclear weapons were game changing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54060,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The bomb dropped on Hiroshima\nreleased a thousand times"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56760,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more energy than the biggest\nconventional explosive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59880,
    "dDurationMs": 2763,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so other countries were\nrightfully concerned."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63630,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the end of the war, Canada and the U.K."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65550,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "requested a meeting to\ndiscuss what would be done"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68220,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about nuclear weapons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69900,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And contrary to what I expected,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72240,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the U.S. was actually\nopen to these discussions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75510,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They realized that they\nwouldn't be the only nation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78060,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with nukes for long."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79920,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they offered to decommission\nall their nuclear weapons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82860,
    "dDurationMs": 2673,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if other nations would\npledge never to make them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88770,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was known as the Baruch plan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91560,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it proposed that an\ninternational body would control"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94290,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all radioactive materials on earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96510,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from mining to refining\nto using these materials"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99840,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for peaceful purposes as a\nnuclear power generation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103230,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the Soviets rejected the proposal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105750,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They saw it as just\nanother ploy to maintain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108240,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "American nuclear dominance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109830,
    "dDurationMs": 3453,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so the global nuclear arms race began."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115560,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To develop new nuclear weapons\nrequired extensive testing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119310,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and most of it was done in\nremote places like the Arctic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122160,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or the South Pacific Islands."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124500,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The U.S. also created a\nnuclear testing site in Nevada,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127620,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the radioactive products of\nwhich blew across the country"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130800,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that outside of Japan, the\npeople most adversely affected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134190,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by American nuclear weapons\nwere Americans themselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138750,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The U.S. soon graduated\nfrom fission weapons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141510,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to thermonuclear bombs which\ncombined fission and fusion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144400,
    "dDurationMs": 2903,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to release even more energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148980,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were as big leap from\nthe first atomic bombs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151440,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as those devices were from\nconventional explosives,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154260,
    "dDurationMs": 2943,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a thousand times again more powerful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157203,
    "dDurationMs": 4497,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Annihilation of any life\non earth has being brought"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161700,
    "dDurationMs": 2947,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "within the range of technical possibility."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168752,
    "dDurationMs": 3028,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Narrator] In 1954 at Bikini\nAtoll in the South Pacific,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171780,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the U.S. tested a new thermonuclear design"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174030,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that used lithium deuteride as a fuel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176880,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they expected the\ndevice code named Shrimp"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178950,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to release the energy equivalent\nof six million tons of TNT"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183480,
    "dDurationMs": 1391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they were wrong."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184871,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(bomb blasts)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189270,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It released two and a half times that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191610,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "due to unanticipated\nreactions with lithium-7."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195210,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as a result, more\nradioactive material was created"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198630,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it rained down over a\nmuch larger area than planned."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202500,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Residents of neighboring\natolls were only evacuated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204930,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "three days later suffering\nfrom radiation sickness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208260,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And further east, the 23 crew\nof a Japanese fishing boat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211410,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were caught in a flurry\nof radioactive white ash."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214920,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And by that evening,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215820,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they were suffering from\nacute radiation syndrome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219210,
    "dDurationMs": 2079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the crew died from\nensuing complications"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221289,
    "dDurationMs": 1208,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "six months later."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222497,
    "dDurationMs": 1577,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Reporter] As a result\nof the extended illness"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224074,
    "dDurationMs": 2719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "brought about by his exposure\nto the radiation fallout."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228690,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- These events triggered public outcry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231090,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "against nuclear testing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232800,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The modern peace sign\nwas designed in the 1950s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235860,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by combining the semaphore\nletters for N and D"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239220,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "standing for nuclear disarmament."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241800,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A number of world leaders\ncalled for a comprehensive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244650,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "test ban, no more testing of\nnuclear weapons by any state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249090,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this call was actually taken seriously"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251880,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the world's nuclear powers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253500,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They entered into negotiations at meetings"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255450,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with very literal names like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257250,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Conference on the Discontinuance\nof Nuclear Weapon Tests"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260550,
    "dDurationMs": 2133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "held in Geneva in 1958."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264060,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to show just how serious they were,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266190,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they even stopped all testing\nduring the negotiations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269220,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is why 1959 is the\nonly year in a long stretch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273420,
    "dDurationMs": 2283,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when no nuclear weapons were detonated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276960,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there was a big\nproblem with negotiating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279360,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a comprehensive test ban\nwhich is how do you know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282750,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the other side will hold\nup their end of the bargain?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286170,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The U.S. worried that the\nSoviets would continue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288540,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "testing covertly and\nleapfrog them technologically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291810,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the Soviets similarly\ndistrusted the U.S.."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295230,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to address these concerns,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296850,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they convened the Conference\nof Experts to Study"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299790,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Possibility of Detecting Violations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302250,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a Possible Agreement on\nSuspension of Nuclear Tests."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306540,
    "dDurationMs": 3963,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Seriously, that was the name,\nI am not making this up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313260,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now detecting atmospheric tests\nwas fairly straightforward."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316830,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The radioactive isotopes\nthey produced disperse"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319440,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the atmosphere and can be detected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321120,
    "dDurationMs": 1863,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thousands of kilometers away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323940,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Underwater tests produce\ndistinctive sounds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326520,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that travel efficiently around\na kilometer below the surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329610,
    "dDurationMs": 3183,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the ocean and these can\nbe picked up by hydrophones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333630,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But underground tests are much\nharder to detect from afar"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337320,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because their radiation\nis mostly contained"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340530,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the Soviets refused to\nallow onsite compliance visits"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343950,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which they regarded as espionage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346290,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is ultimately why when\na test ban treaty was signed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349800,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 1963, it was only a partial ban."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353670,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It banned testing underwater,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355410,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the atmosphere and in space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357450,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "places where compliance could be verified,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359670,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it didn't ban testing\nunderground for the simple reason"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363030,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it was almost impossible\nto verify compliance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366330,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But scientists had been\ntrying to find a way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368730,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to reliably detect\nunderground detonations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371700,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Following the Geneva meeting,\nAmerican and Soviet scientists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374640,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "formed a working group\nto discuss the issue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377400,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and their idea was to\nuse seismometers located"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380190,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outside the countries where\nnukes were being tested"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382680,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to detect the faint ground\nvibrations caused by explosions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 387210,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem was how do you\ndistinguish a nuclear test"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390570,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from an earthquake?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392340,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every day around the world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393480,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are close to 300 earthquakes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395670,
    "dDurationMs": 2193,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a magnitude of three or greater."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399300,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In addition, part of\nthe purpose of detecting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401760,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your adversaries tests is to spy on them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404460,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to know how big of an\nexplosion they can make."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407490,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the seismometer signal\ndepends not only on the yield"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410400,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the device but also on\nhow deep it was buried."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414360,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For a given yield, deeper\nexplosions appear smaller."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418620,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So scientists wanted a\nmethod to reliably determine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421500,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whether a given signal was\na bomb or an earthquake"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424530,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if it was a bomb, how big it was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426990,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how deep it was buried."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429240,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They knew that all this\ninformation was contained"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431850,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the seismometer signal but\nit couldn't just be read off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435210,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by looking at the squiggles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436800,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They needed to know how much\nof different frequencies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439740,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were present which meant\nthey needed to take"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442740,
    "dDurationMs": 1773,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a Fourier transform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445860,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A Fourier transform is a\nway of decomposing a signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448860,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into pure sine waves, each\nwith its own amplitude"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452220,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and frequency that add to make it up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455580,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This seems a bit like magic since the sum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458250,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a set of sine waves can\nlook arbitrarily complicated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460890,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and nothing like its component parts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464040,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are some elegant ways to understand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466230,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how Fourier transforms work,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467850,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shout out to the awesome\nvideo by 3Blue1Brown."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470730,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I wanna take more of\na brute force approach."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473820,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you wanna know how much\nof a particular sine wave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476700,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is in a signal, just multiply\nthe signal by the sine wave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480240,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at each point and then add\nup the area under the curve."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485130,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a simple example, say our\nsignal is just a sine wave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488670,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a certain frequency but\npretend we don't know that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491520,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we're trying to figure out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492930,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which sine waves add to make it up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495600,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, if you multiply\nthis signal by a sine wave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497910,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of an arbitrary frequency, the\ntwo waves are uncorrelated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502110,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You're just as likely to\nfind places where they have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503850,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same sign, both\npositive or both negative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506880,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as where they have opposite\nsigns and therefore"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509610,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when you multiply them together,\nthe area above the x-axis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512970,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is equal to the area below the x-axis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515490,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So these areas add up to zero which means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518880,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that frequency sine wave is\nnot a part of your signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522630,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this will be true for\nalmost all frequencies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525120,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could try assuming you're looking over"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526920,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a long enough timeframe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528630,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only exception is if the\nfrequency of the sine wave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531900,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exactly matches that of the signal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535080,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now these waves are correlated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537750,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so their product is always\npositive and so is the area"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541020,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "under the curve that indicates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542910,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that this sine wave is part of our signal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546390,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this trick works even\nif the signal is composed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548820,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a bunch of different frequencies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550830,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the sine waves frequency\nis one of the components"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553560,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the signal it will\ncorrelate with the signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555750,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "producing a non-zero area."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557850,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the size of this area tells\nyou the relative amplitude"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560940,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of that frequency sine wave in the signal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564060,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Repeat this process for all\nfrequencies of sine waves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567300,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you get the frequency spectrum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569190,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Essentially which frequencies are present"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571500,
    "dDurationMs": 1893,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in what proportions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575580,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now so far I've only\ntalked about sine waves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578250,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but if the signal is a cosine wave,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580800,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then even if you multiply\nit by a sine wave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582810,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the exact same frequency,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584640,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the area under the curve will be zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587400,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So for each frequency,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588690,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we actually need to\nmultiply by a sine wave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591420,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a cosine wave and find\nthe amplitudes for each."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595530,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The ratio of these amplitudes\nindicates the phase"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598830,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the signal that is\nhow much it's shifted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601320,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the left or to the right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603330,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can calculate these\nsine and cosine amplitudes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605820,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "separately or you can use Euler's formula"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609570,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you only need to multiply your signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611160,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by one exponential term."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613440,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then the real part of the\nsum is the cosine amplitude"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616380,
    "dDurationMs": 3213,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the imaginary part\nis the sine amplitude."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620790,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the American delegation\nat the Geneva meeting,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622980,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there was a physicist, Richard Garwin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624870,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a mathematician John Tukey."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627120,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They got into a debate\nwith the Soviet delegation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629640,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over which nation's\nseismometers were superior."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632700,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Garwin simulated the responses\nof both countries' devices"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636780,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a computer at CERN."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639000,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The next day, everyone agreed\nthere wasn't much difference."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 643500,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The real obstacle to detecting\nunderground explosions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646860,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wasn't the accuracy of the seismometers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649170,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was the vast amounts\nof computation required"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651690,
    "dDurationMs": 2823,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to Fourier transform\nthe seismometer signals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656160,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's an example seismometer signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658200,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and its Fourier transform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660150,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus far I've been thinking about signals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662430,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as infinite continuous waves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664650,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when you take their Fourier transform,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666300,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get an infinite\ncontinuous frequency spectrum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669960,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But real world signals are not like that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672240,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are finite and made\nup of individual samples"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674940,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or data points."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676440,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though a seismometer\nsignal looks smooth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679050,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and continuous, it doesn't\nrecord ground motion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682200,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with infinite precision."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684180,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is some fundamental\ngraininess to the data"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687270,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so what you have is discreet finite data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690900,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can't use the\nidealized Fourier transform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694890,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, you have to perform something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697110,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called a Discreet Fourier Transform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700110,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And one of the distinguishing features"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702060,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a Discreet Fourier Transform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703860,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that the frequency spectrum\nis also discreet and finite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708270,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can think of the frequencies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709650,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as falling into a finite number of bins."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713370,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what determines the\nnumber and size of these bins"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716370,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the number of samples in the signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718290,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how closely spaced they are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720810,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, the more\nspaced out the samples are,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723960,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the lower the maximum\nfrequency you can measure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726660,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because the samples aren't\nclose enough together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728790,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to capture high frequency oscillations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732030,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the shorter the duration of the signal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734400,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the harder it is to tell\nsimilar frequencies apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737520,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this lowers the frequency resolution."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740550,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The shorter the signal, the\nwider each frequency bin is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 745230,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The lowest non-zero frequency\nyou can effectively measure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748950,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is one whose period is equal\nto the duration of the signal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752850,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the higher frequency bins\nare just integer multiples"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755880,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of this frequency."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756990,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they fit two, three,\nfour, and so on periods"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760620,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the duration of the signal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762690,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The total number of\nfrequency bins is equal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766200,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the number of samples in the signal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768570,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if the signal is made\nup of eight samples,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771030,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the transform has\neight frequency bins"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 773760,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going from zero up to seven\ntimes the fundamental frequency."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778530,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's do an example."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780540,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Say we have a signal\nmade up of eight samples."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783960,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, then the discrete Fourier transform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 785940,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will have eight frequency bins."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788460,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first bin corresponds\nto a frequency of zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791940,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Essentially this measures if the signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793950,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is systematically shifted off the x-axis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 797250,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can think of it as\nmeasuring the DC offset."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800670,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You multiply each data point by one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803070,
    "dDurationMs": 3603,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and add them all together, in\nthis case, they add to zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808290,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second frequency bin\ncorresponds to the frequency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811260,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that fits one period in\nthe duration of the signal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814590,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in this case that\ncorresponds to one hertz."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817740,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You multiply each point by a\nsine wave of this frequency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821610,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a cosine wave of this frequency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824430,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and separately add them up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826740,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For sine, they add to zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828780,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For cosine, they add to four"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831390,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then repeat the process\nfor two hertz, three hertz,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834840,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so on, up to seven hertz."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837390,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you have the discreet\nFourier transform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840570,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of this really simple signal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842970,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now this process works fine in principle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845730,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you could use it to calculate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 847530,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all discrete Fourier transforms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849900,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the problem is it requires\nway too many calculations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854160,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To complete one discrete Fourier transform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856590,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "requires multiplying N data points"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858810,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by N different frequency waves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861360,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So N squared complex multiplications."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 864990,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now this is doable for eight samples"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867390,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but if you had say a million samples,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870180,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that would require a million squared"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872250,
    "dDurationMs": 3003,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or one trillion calculations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 877350,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the speed of 1960s computers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879750,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that would take over\nthree years to complete,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882330,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all for a single transform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884580,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now a million samples is\nadmittedly more than you would need"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887520,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a single seismic event\nbut to analyze tens of events"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 890910,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "per day from hundreds of seismometers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 893160,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it would just be far too time consuming"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895590,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's what gave\nscientists the impetus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897630,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to look for a better way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899850,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the breakthrough\ncame in 1963 at a meeting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902490,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the President's Science\nAdvisory Committee."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904950,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "President John F. Kennedy was there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906750,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as were Garwin and Tukey,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908250,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the physicist and mathematician\nfrom the Geneva meeting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911340,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Although they were discussing\nissues of national importance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914130,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the Apollo program and\nnuclear fallout shelters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 917250,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the meeting was apparently pretty boring."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 919830,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Garwin observed Tukey doodling throughout"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 923130,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but what he was actually doing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925020,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was working on discreet\nFourier transforms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928440,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the end of the meeting,\nGarwin asked Tukey"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930390,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what he had worked out and\nhe was shocked to learn"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933330,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Tukey knew a way to compute\ndiscreet Fourier transforms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936600,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with many fewer computations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939090,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would mean that the\ncalculation that would've taken"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940950,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over three years could be\ndone in just 35 minutes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 945120,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This has aptly become known\nas the Fast Fourier Transform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949260,
    "dDurationMs": 2193,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So here is how it works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 953940,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Consider the example from\nbefore with eight samples."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956670,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each of those data\npoints must be multiplied"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958470,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the eight different frequency waves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960810,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here I'm only showing\ncosines for simplicity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 964260,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you would expect this to\nrequire eight times eight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966990,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or 64 complex multiplication."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970020,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But due to the periodic\nnature of sinusoids,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973170,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these waves of different frequencies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975330,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "overlap in a predictable way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977970,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, at the middle data point,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 980520,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of the four odd\nfrequencies have the same value"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983670,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and all of the four even frequencies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 985770,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have the same value as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987270,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So instead of doing eight multiplication,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989970,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you only need to do two."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992130,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this sort of duplication occurs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993870,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the other data points as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995910,
    "dDurationMs": 4863,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So instead of performing 64\ncalculations, you need only 24."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001700,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that might seem\nlike a small improvement"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004070,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's the difference\nbetween a calculation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006020,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that scales as N, the\nnumber of samples squared"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1009260,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "versus one that scales\nas Nlog base two of N"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1012980,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means the bigger the data set,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1014870,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the greater the savings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016940,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A signal with a thousand\nsamples would require"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019820,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "100 times fewer calculations\nand a million samples"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1023900,
    "dDurationMs": 3723,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would require 50,000\ntimes fewer calculations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028580,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how do you know which\ncalculations are redundant?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032900,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, take your samples and split them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035510,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into even and odd index points."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038900,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You still need to multiply"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040040,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each of these by the eight\ndifferent frequency waves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043370,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now let's look only at\nthe even points and compare"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1046940,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the first four frequencies to\nthe second four frequencies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1051290,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what you find is that in each case"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053930,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the location of the samples,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1055730,
    "dDurationMs": 3153,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the values of the two\nsine waves are the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1059840,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A similar pattern can be\nobserved for the odd index points"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1063620,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "except the values of one\nsine wave are the negative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066860,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1067940,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More generally, they're\nrelated by a complex number."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071510,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what this means is\nthat you don't have to do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1074900,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the multiplication for the second half"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077180,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the frequencies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1078680,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once you've calculated\nthe odd and even sums"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1081620,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the lower half the frequencies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083720,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can reuse these values\nto find the upper half."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088160,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you've effectively cut\nthe number of calculations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1090950,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "required in half but that's\nonly a factor of two,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1095270,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how do you get down to Nlog base two of N?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1098480,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, you repeat the same trick,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1100670,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "split the samples again\ninto even an odd points"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1104420,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then again repeatedly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106910,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "until you're down to single data points."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110030,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At each split, you can\nexploit the symmetries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112730,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of sinusoidal functions to\ncut the number of calculations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1115850,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in half."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1117140,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that is how the Fast\nFourier Transform reduces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1120230,
    "dDurationMs": 3003,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "N squared calculations down to NlogN."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1124070,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's why today whenever anyone takes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1125930,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a Fourier transform,\nit's almost always done"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128960,
    "dDurationMs": 2163,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a Fast Fourier Transform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1132110,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Garwin approached an IBM\nresearcher, James Cooley"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134960,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to program a computer\nto run the FFT algorithm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138200,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but he didn't tell him\nthe reason was to detect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140540,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "underground Soviet nuclear tests."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142370,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He said it was to work out the spins"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144020,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a crystal of helium-3."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1146240,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cooley and Tukey published the algorithm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1148370,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a seminal 1965 paper and\nits use immediately took off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1153590,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it was too late to secure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1156110,
    "dDurationMs": 1983,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a comprehensive nuclear test ban."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159129,
    "dDurationMs": 2831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By that time, the U.K., France and China"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1161960,
    "dDurationMs": 3393,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had joined the Soviet Union\nand the U.S. as nuclear powers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1167060,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the partial test ban treaty,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1168890,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "far from deescalating\nthe nuclear arms race"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171560,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just sent it underground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1173780,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The thinking was if you were only allowed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1175700,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to test underground, then you\nbetter be testing extensively"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1179000,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so as not to fall behind all\nthe other nuclear states."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1182420,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So from 1963, 1,500 nuclear\nweapons were detonated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1187040,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's roughly one a week for 30 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1190970,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This testing facilitated the construction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1192980,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of an absurd number of nukes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1195380,
    "dDurationMs": 1781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the peak in the mid 1980s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1197161,
    "dDurationMs": 4189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "70,000 nuclear warheads were in existence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1201350,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Total expenditure on\nnukes in the 20th century"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1203840,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is estimated at around $10\ntrillion each for the U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the Soviet Union\nadjusting for inflation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1211280,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If only scientists had been\nconfident in their ability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1214010,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to remotely detect underground\ntests in the early 1960s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1217430,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then a comprehensive test\nban could have been reached,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1220220,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stopping the nuclear arms race\nbefore it really got going."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1224390,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To check how realistic this is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1226580,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I asked Richard Garwin himself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1229430,
    "dDurationMs": 1383,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Well, it's a good story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1232123,
    "dDurationMs": 1479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It is a good story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1233602,
    "dDurationMs": 3928,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It would've helped and it\nmight have turned the tide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1237530,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But that would've required\nan earlier discovery"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1240020,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the Fast Fourier Transform\nand as luck would have it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1243680,
    "dDurationMs": 3513,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was discovered earlier\nbut then forgotten."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1248090,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All the way back in 1805,\nMathematician Carl Friedrich Gauss"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1251750,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was studying the newly\ndiscovered asteroids"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253790,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Pallas, Ceres and Juno."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1256340,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To determine the orbit of Juno,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1257930,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gauss devised a novel\napproach to harmonic analysis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1260870,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he jotted it down in his notes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1262730,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but later used a different method"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1264800,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he never thought to\npublish that first insight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1267830,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today we can see that\nGauss had figured out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1270470,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the discreet Fourier Transform\nbefore Joseph Fourier himself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1273890,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "published it in 1807."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1275900,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And he had developed the\nsame Fast Fourier Transform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1278960,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "algorithm as Cooley and Tukey\na century and a half earlier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1283880,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The reason his breakthrough\nwas not widely adopted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285980,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was because it only appeared\nafter his death in volume three"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1289460,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of his collected works and it\nwas written with non-standard"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1292520,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "notation in a 19th\ncentury version of Latin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1296480,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What do you think would've\nhappened if Gauss had realized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299060,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the significance of his\ndiscovery and had published it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1301730,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a way that others could understand?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1304160,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With our modern network of seismometers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1306260,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and computing and the\nFast Fourier Transform,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1308810,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "today, we have the ability to\ndetect magnitude three events"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1311930,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which correspond to a one\nkilo ton or so explosion,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1315530,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "basically anywhere on earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1318320,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Following Cooley and Tukey's\npaper, the use of FFTs exploded"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1322460,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they are the basis for\nmost compression algorithms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1325340,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the ones that allow you to watch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1326840,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and listen to this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1329210,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's how the Fast Fourier Transform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1330950,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "allows you to compress an image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1333290,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You take the pixel brightness\nvalues for each row"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1336740,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of an image and perform\na Fast Fourier transform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1340880,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So essentially, you're\nfiguring out what frequencies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1343640,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are present in the brightness values"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1346100,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the rows of an image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1347930,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, brightness represents the magnitude"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1350150,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of each frequency component and the color"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1352400,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "represents the phase, how\nshifted that frequency is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1355250,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the left or the right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1357020,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then you perform another\nFFT for the columns of pixels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1362090,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It doesn't matter if you do\nthe rows or columns first,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1365300,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which you need is a two dimensional FFT"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1368570,
    "dDurationMs": 1263,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the original image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1370700,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For almost all real world images,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1373460,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you find that a lot of the\nvalues in the transform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1376280,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are close to zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1378200,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've taken the log of the transform values"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380150,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you can see them but if\nI don't, then it's clear"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1383030,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most of the values,\nespecially toward the edges"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1385280,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are very small and these\ncorrespond to high frequencies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1390140,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what this means is\nthat you can throw out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1392540,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lot of the information\nin the transformed image"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1395180,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say 99% of it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1397520,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when you invert that result,\nyou still get a fairly good"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401630,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "representation of the original image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1404570,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So on your computer, most\nof the images will be saved"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1407540,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in this form as a two dimensional\nFast Fourier Transform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1410750,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then when you wanna\nlook at the picture again,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1412730,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the computer simply inverts the transform."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1416390,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are so many applications for FFTs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1418880,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from solving differential\nequations to radar and sonar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1422600,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "studying crystal structures, WiFi and 5G."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1425780,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Basically all kinds of\nsignal processing use FFTs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1429800,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's why mathematician\nGilbert Strang called the FFT"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432950,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the most important numerical\nalgorithm of our lifetime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1436760,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If only it had become more widely adopted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1439340,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after Gauss discovered it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1440900,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the FFT may have even more dramatically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1443810,
    "dDurationMs": 1893,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "transformed our world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1451130,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I don't think Gauss\ncould ever have imagined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1453320,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how important the FFT would be,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1455390,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just as most people don't think\nabout the cumulative impact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1458360,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their life's work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1459890,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know in an average career,\nyou work 40 hours a week,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1463040,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "50 weeks a year for 40 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1465680,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that works out to 80,000 hours."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1468890,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It means that your career might\nbe your biggest opportunity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1472130,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make a difference in the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1473870,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what do you wanna\ndo with all that time?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1476750,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the name of this video\nsponsor is 80,000 Hours"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1480290,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "referencing the amount\nof impact you can have,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1482600,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the amount of hours you spend at work,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1484430,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they are not selling anything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486370,
    "dDurationMs": 2590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "80,000 Hours is a\nnonprofit that helps people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1488960,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "find fulfilling careers\nthat make a positive impact."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1492050,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The typical advice from career\ncenters or aptitude tests"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1495020,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really just focuses on finding a job"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1496790,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that fits your personal preferences."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1498650,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what if you care\nmore about doing good?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1501530,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, they won't really\nknow what to tell you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1503000,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "besides a few well known professions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1504710,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like being a doctor or a teacher."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1506930,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When I finished college, I knew\nI liked filmmaking, teaching"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1510380,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and science and that I wanted\nto have a big positive impact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1513620,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but YouTube didn't exist yet\nand so I honestly had no idea"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1517100,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what I was gonna do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1518420,
    "dDurationMs": 2898,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I feel really fortunate\nto be able to do something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1521318,
    "dDurationMs": 1902,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every day that I both enjoy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1523220,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and which makes a positive\nimpact on the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1525830,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So believe me, there are\na lot of things out there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1528320,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that you can do and 80,000\nHours offers tons of resources"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1531590,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to help you find those things."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1533090,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From research backed guides\non how to pick a career"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1535790,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that tackles pressing issues"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1537440,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a regular newsletter and podcast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1539840,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They even have a curated job\nboard that's kept up to date"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1542870,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with hundreds of jobs they\nthink will make an impact."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1545930,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have done over 10 years\nof research alongside academics"
    } ]
